    {
      "id": "e0a35b87-fd4e-44b1-bbd0-57b005dd6c85",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 760,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## Setup\n1. **Settings** node: TTS endpoint URL + model + the two voice IDs, Bunny storage URL (`https://storage.bunnycdn.com/<zone>`, or your region host) and pull-zone base URL. Check `ghostUrl`.\n2. Credentials (Templated Custom Auth): **Qwen TTS** → `{\"headers\":{\"Authorization\":\"Bearer {{api_key}}\"}}`. **Upload to Bunny** → `{\"headers\":{\"AccessKey\":\"{{api_key}}\"}}` with the storage zone password.\n3. Ghost Admin → Integrations → custom integration → two webhooks to the production URL of **Ghost Webhook**:\n   - *Post published* → `...?event=published`\n   - *Published post updated* → `...?event=edited`\n4. Tags: `#audio` opts a post in. `#audio-refresh` regenerates after edits (removed automatically). `#lang-es` or a slug ending in `-es` picks La Operadora.\n\nText edited without `#audio-refresh` keeps the old audio and retitles the card as an earlier version. The endpoint must be OpenAI-compatible `/audio/speech` returning MP3."
      }
    }
  ],
